From 9d8f5559926d17952ce8569043f3dcd42664db82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 11:09:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08113/11362] [outer-loop] ARC goal-evidence A/B: the two
 shipped goal knobs are aimed at the wrong 20% of cells

Measures whether attaching the agent's own observed transitions to the goal-only
induction prompt (CARNOT_ARC_GOAL_PROMPT_TRANSITIONS) and de-shadowing the
predicate (CARNOT_ARC_GOAL_DEDUP) stop the model DECLINING to write a win
condition. Primary is mechanical AST predicate shape, NOT plan_found and NOT the
goal gate -- plan_found is an exact function of the gate's kind, so grading a goal
intervention with it grades the gate using the gate.

HONEST HEADLINE: a NON-TEST on the primary, not a null. Truncated by its own
stopping rule at 17 of 140 cells, so the primary stands on one paired game against
a design powered on twenty. Nothing is claimed about the declined rate.

What does not depend on that n:
- The knobs are STRUCTURALLY MISDIRECTED. Pre-flight over 116 frozen engines,
  before any GPU time: DECLINED is 0.495 on combined-path cells and 0.174 on
  split-induce cells, and split-induce is 19.8% of cells. Both knobs live only in
  the split fallback, so 46 of 50 declines are unreachable by either flag and the
  live-path ceiling is 3.4 points. Declared before running.
- The evidence-carrying goal prompt hits the generation cap: 4096/4096 tokens vs
  the control's 314, tail degenerating into 819 empty python fences, live cells
  failing with a truncated definition. Median goal call 3s -> 343s.
- A fixed generator seed does NOT fix the completion on this server. The harness's
  own byte-identity check fired: same seed, no goal-only call in any arm, control
  3722 bytes vs both treatments 4150. B and C match 2/2, so it is KV-cache
  position, not the knob. The seeded pairing is approximate and arm order is a
  confound on shape, not only timing. The harness comment asserting the opposite
  has been corrected in place rather than left standing.

Also self-reported: GROUNDED is partially determined by the treatment; the primary
and TROPE are not. The pre-registered rule was not changed after seeing data -- a
labelled post-hoc sensitivity is reported beside it.

Captured completions are stored as .py.txt so ruff-format cannot rewrite the
evidence that engine_sha256 commits to.

Defaults unchanged: both knobs still ship OFF. adversarial_verify 0-flagged.
No scored or online ARC game was played; submission is operator-only.

